{
  "slug": "idea-map",
  "version": "1",
  "name": {
    "en": "Idea Map",
    "zh-CN": "概念图"
  },
  "line": "A concept map set in type on a cool layout sheet: every term stands on its own underline, the underline runs on as the line to the next term, and how that line is drawn is the relation (an arrow causes, a dashed line contributes, chevrons lead to, dots are part of, a T-bar blocks, a double line opposes); the camera rides each new line to the term it reaches.",
  "scenarios": ["lesson", "report"],
  "tags": ["line-art", "minimal", "modern", "light"],
  "uses": [
    "cycles and processes in science and nature",
    "causes and effects in history and current affairs",
    "root-cause reviews of incidents and failures",
    "how the parts of a system, an organisation or an argument relate",
    "policies and decisions with their side effects"
  ],
